    {
        "n":  24,
        "title":  "Trauma Scoring Systems -",
        "text":  "Several scoring systems are used to classify trauma patients and predict the outcome. Following are some of the commonly used scoring systems – \nRevised Trauma Score – \nCalculated from sum of Patient’s Respiratory rate, Systolic BP and GCS. \nScore ranges from 0 to 12 \nHelps in triage as 12 is labelled Green (delayed Rx), 11 as Yellow (urgent) and 0-10 as Red (Immediate)\n2. Mangled Extremity Severity Score – \nScore used to predict chances of amputation after severe extremity trauma.\nContains 4 variables – Skeletal and soft tissue injury, Ishemia of limb, Shock and Age.",
        "notes":  ""
    },
    {
        "n":  25,
        "title":  "Ganga Hospital Open Injury Severity Score -",
        "text":  "Assesses 3 areas – Skin and Fascia, the musculotendinous unit and the Bones.",
        "notes":  ""
